Statement: "The citation check is right to report that both sentences are supported by source [4]."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'False. The first sentence is supported by [4]. The second claims 30 days and cites [4], but [4] has no number at all: 30 comes from [3], the general refund policy. A citation check that searches the whole context instead of the cited source passes this sentence, which is why its pass rate rose (E) while answers got worse. The model filled the gap with the closest number it had and attached the wrong citation - a generation error the check should have flagged.', 5, 5
    WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM challenge.questions WHERE challenge_id = (SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_quiz_py_rag_331') AND order_index = 5)
    RETURNING id
)
